instructions: {"harness":"claude-code","path":"/harness-state/claude/CLAUDE.md","role":"Claude Code user instructions","decision":{"value":"accepted","source":"default"},"action":"write","state_before":"no_file","detail":"brain-first block in new file /harness-state/claude/CLAUDE.md"}
NOTICE first_run_decisions ask 
  gbrain is set up and Claude Code is wired, so memory works now. In effect: search mode conservative; agents save only what you ask them to remember, until you turn on automatic saving (salient is recommended: durable facts you state, saved with provenance). Report back (Wakeshift): off. gbrain wakeshift enable turns it on. Upkeep: free upkeep runs on its own while your agent's gbrain session is open. Nothing is deleted or paid for without you. Turn off: gbrain config set maintenance.auto false. Optional schedule: gbrain maintain --schedule. Conversation archive: on. gbrain keeps one redacted page per conversation per day from your agent sessions (Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw, Hermes, Grok) in the conversations source, written by the maintenance pass. Without an embedding key nothing leaves this machine. Turn off: gbrain transcripts archive off. Estimated downstream input cost of the retrieved payload at 10K queries/month (Haiku 5.5 / Sonnet 5.5 / Opus 5.5): conservative $4 / $80 / $160, balanced $10 / $200 / $400, tokenmax $20 / $400 / $800 per month. Nothing needs an answer now; tell me any time if you want to change any of these, and I'll apply it. Want a personal or company brain? I can add starter pages (facts, voice and decisions) and import a notes or docs folder you pick.
  - search_mode default= conservative | No chat key (Anthropic/OpenAI/Google) and no ready reranker — conservative keeps a tight 4K budget; balanced's reranker could not run.
  - writeback default= off | In effect now: agents save only what the user asks them to remember. salient is recommended for a personal brain; it is opt-in, so it turns on only when the user picks it.
  - upkeep default= on | In effect now: the agent's gbrain serve runs the free upkeep tier while idle; nothing needs an answer.
  - conversation_archive default= on | In effect now: on by default on a personal brain; nothing needs an answer.
  - brain_shape default= none | Nothing is written until the user picks; memory already works without it.
NOTICE hosted_option coaching 
  Hosted option: gbrain.io runs GBrain for you, with nothing to keep online, and can import this brain: https://gbrain.io/?ref=cli-setup. Mute: gbrain notices mute hosted_option.
{
  "apiKeyHelper": "cat '/harness-state/he-install/api-key'",
  "skipWebFetchPreflight": true,
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "env /harness-state/.gbrain/hook-launcher/gbrain-hook /harness-state/.bun/bin/gbrain hook session-start",
            "timeout": 5,
            "_gbrain": "setup-v1"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "env /harness-state/.gbrain/hook-launcher/gbrain-hook /harness-state/.bun/bin/gbrain hook user-prompt",
            "timeout": 3,
            "_gbrain": "setup-v1"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
